# {DOMAIN} SCRATCHPAD
<!-- OPT-IN. Only create this file for complex or stateful domains. -->
<!-- NOT a universal mandatory doc. Do not create unless the domain accumulates -->
<!-- decisions-with-rationale and live state that have nowhere else to live. -->
<!-- Good candidates: architecture domains, bot frameworks, financial pipelines, -->
<!-- any domain where the same design decisions recur across sessions. -->
<!-- Example filename: HEALTH_JOURNAL_SHARED.md (Health + Journal domains sharing -->
<!-- a vocabulary) - see A_B_SHARED.md.template for the cross-domain pattern. -->

<!-- SIZE CAP: 150 lines / 6,000 chars = scout threshold. -->
<!--   At or under: main session direct-reads. -->
<!--   Over: dispatch a Scout with a fixed return format: -->
<!--         1. Current state - 3-5 bullets -->
<!--         2. Open loops - max 5 lines -->
<!--         3. Last 3 decisions with 1-line rationale -->
<!--         No session narrative in the scout return. -->
<!--   Over 200 lines = OVER CAP: scout fires but carries "(OVER CAP - prune on wrap)"; -->
<!--         overflow archives to {DOMAIN}_SCRATCHPAD_ARCHIVE.md. -->

<!-- WRITE DISCIPLINE: write at session END (wrap) only. -->
<!--   During-session scratch goes to ephemeral working scratchpads (different contract). -->
<!--   DISTILL TEST at wrap: task -> QUEUE, settled decision -> trunk, cross-domain finding -> shared knowledge store. -->
<!--   What survives: only live state and unresolved design thinking. -->
<!--   GUARDRAIL: grew 30+ lines this session? Distill pass MANDATORY before commit. -->
<!--              If context too tight to distill: write "DISTILL PENDING" at the very top. -->

<!-- BRIGHT LINE vs HANDOFF: -->
<!--   HANDOFF = session baton (what THIS session did, in-flight, blocked). -->
<!--   SCRATCHPAD = domain state board (what the domain IS and WHY, across all sessions). -->
<!--   As durable state migrates here, HANDOFF SHRINKS. They are subtractive, not additive. -->
<!--   A HANDOFF block surviving 3+ sessions unmoved belongs here instead. -->

<!-- DISTINCT FROM {DOMAIN}_PROGRESS.md: PROGRESS.md is the context-shield emergency save -->
<!-- (fire when context is critically full mid-session). Scratchpad is the structured wrap artifact. -->

